course: dictionary
lesson: 6002
title: Meaty: one word, three meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The sentence around the word tells you which meaning to use. Meaty is one of these words: it can describe food, a strong body, or a book full of ideas.
explain: «Hedgehogs should not be given milk; leave out water and meaty cat or dog food instead.» Here the food is the clue. Meaty means full of meat, or tasting of meat. Try it in the sentence: meat food is safe for hedgehogs, so the meaning fits.
explain: «Her meaty arms» would describe someone who is big, thick and strong. In school talk, a meaty question is one that is hard and interesting to think about. Always ask: which meaning fits the other words in this sentence?
fact: Meaty can describe food, a strong body, or an interesting idea.
fact: «Meaty» means full of meat or tasting of meat, as in «a meaty stew».
fact: «Meaty» can also mean big, thick and strong, as in «meaty arms».
fact: «Meaty» can mean full of interesting, important ideas, as in «a meaty book».
fact: Meatier and meatiest are the comparison forms, as in «a meatier stew» and «the meatiest bone».
exercise: «Milk is bad for hedgehogs, which can get very ill; a dish of water and meaty cat or dog food are safe.» What does meaty mean here? | Full of interesting ideas | Big, thick and strong | *Full of meat, or tasting of meat | Wet and cold
exercise: Ben says, «That wrestler has meaty arms.» What does meaty mean in this sentence? | Full of meat | Soft and smooth | *Big, thick and strong | Full of interesting ideas
exercise: Mrs Chen says, «That was a meaty book, full of ideas to think about.» What does meaty mean here? | Greasy and wet | Very quiet and gentle | *Full of interesting, important ideas | Tasting of meat
test: «The dog chewed a meaty bone.» What does meaty mean here? | Full of interesting ideas | Very hungry | *Full of meat | Big, thick and strong
test: Priya says, «That is a meaty question.» What does meaty mean? | Quick and easy | Full of meat | *Hard and interesting to think about | Big and thick
exam: Which meaning of meaty fits «Hedgehogs wake from hibernation thin and hungry; a shallow dish of water and meaty cat food helps them»? | *Full of meat, or tasting of meat | Full of interesting ideas | Big, thick and strong | Cold and wet
